also has a mission to educate people in general about tsunamis, including the 2004 Indian Ocean earthquake and tsunami.","wpu":"Pacific Tsunami Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Hilo_Pacific_Tsnumai_Museum_Big_island_Hawaii_Park_%2846226726062%29.jpg/960px-Hilo_Pacific_Tsnumai_Museum_Big_island_Hawaii_Park_%2846226726062%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mokupāpapa Discovery Center","g":"sights","k":"aquarium","la":19.726674,"lo":-155.086979,"d":2847,"h":"Tu-Sa 09:00-16:00","w":"https://www.papahanaumokuakea.gov/education/center.html","ph":"+1 808 498 4709"},{"n":"Kenyan K. Beale Community Robotics Center","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":19.726716,"lo":-155.087005,"d":2850,"h":"Sa 10:00-14:00","w":"https://hawaiisciencemuseum.org/kenyan-k-beals-community-robotics-center/"},{"n":"Hawaii Science and Technology Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":19.725959,"lo":-155.088238,"d":2989,"w":"https://hawaiisciencemuseum.org/","ph":"+1 808-731-4476"},{"n":"East Hawaiʻi Cultural Center","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":19.724764,"lo":-155.088211,"d":3009,"h":"Tu-Fr 10:00-16:00; Sa 10:00-14:00","w":"https://www.ehcc.org/","ds":"The East Hawaiʻi Cultural Center (EHCC) is an art gallery, community theater, and cultural center in downtown Hilo, Hawaii. EHCC features regular art exhibitions with free or suggested donation entry to the general public. Founded by an umbrella group of local arts organizations, the Center is housed in a historic former police station facing Kalakaua Park.","wpu":"East Hawaiʻi Cultural Center","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/East_Hawaii_Cultural_Center.jpg/960px-East_Hawaii_Cultural_Center.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Naha Stone","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":19.724451,"lo":-155.090553,"d":3256,"ds":"The Naha Stone is a large volcanic rock located in Hilo, Hawaii. The stone was used in the cultural traditions of Native Hawaiians, and many legends surround it. It is estimated to weigh between 2.5 and 3.5 tons.","wpu":"Naha Stone","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Naha_Stone%2C_Hilo.jpg/960px-Naha_Stone%2C_Hilo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lyman Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":19.722184,"lo":-155.090702,"d":3329,"h":"Mo-Fr 10:00-16:30; PH off","w":"https://lymanmuseum.com"},{"n":"Lyman House Memorial Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":19.722031,"lo":-155.091014,"d":3364,"ds":"The Lyman House Memorial Museum, also known as the Lyman Museum and Lyman House, is a Hilo, Hawaii-based natural history museum founded in 1931 in the Lyman family mission house, originally built in 1838. The main collections were moved to an adjacent modern building in the 1960s, while the house is open for tours as the island's oldest surviving wood-framed building.","wpu":"Lyman House Memorial Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Lyman_House_Museum%2C_Hilo.jpg/960px-Lyman_House_Museum%2C_Hilo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Scenic Point","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":19.742407,"lo":-155.090218,"d":3450},{"n":"Honoli‘i Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":19.755171,"lo":-155.091109,"d":4293},{"n":"Rainbow Falls Lookout","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":19.719303,"lo":-155.108386,"d":5202},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":19.722471,"lo":-155.0647,"d":971},{"n":"Mail With Us","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":19.720633,"lo":-155.064557,"d":1145},{"n":"FedEx Ship Center","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":19.716299,"lo":-155.051434,"d":1767},{"n":"United States Post Office","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":19.716147,"lo":-155.050329,"d":1843},{"n":"CU Hawaii","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":19.715465,"lo":-155.069,"d":1870},{"n":"Hilt Bitcoin ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la